  "reading_notes": [
    "Theorem 11.0.2 uses a complete manifold and a global Ricci lower bound. It does not itself assert the ball-local version requested by the platform milestone.",
    "On printed page 197, the displayed limit of the unnormalized radial density needs normalization: for n>1 its model behaves as t^(n-1), while the ratio to model density tends to one. No unnormalized limit of one is adopted here.",
    "The Riccati trace argument divides by n-1, so its eventual formal use must distinguish dimension one.",
    "The Ricci coefficient is (n-1)*K for model sectional curvature K. RicciBoundedBelowOn takes the Ricci coefficient as its argument."
  ],
